# Session Handover — the Measured Crossing [SPEC:HANDOVER-PROCESS]

> The `handover` skill (`.claude/skills/handover/SKILL.md`), lifted into the corpus as a queryable spec. David's principle (2026-07-22): do not leave the crossing headroom to subjective interpretation on either side — MEASURE what the handover actually costs. The ritual stamps its own boundaries so the retrospective computes its true context cost into SQLite (`sessions.handover_cost_pct`), and the compact-threshold becomes data-driven rather than guessed. This is the DUSK half of the boot read's DAWN ([SBR-ZEALOUS-CONTRIBUTION] — boot reads, dusk writes).

---

## 1. Why this is a ritual, not a reflex

### [HANDOVER-IS-MEASURED] The crossing is stamped so its cost is data, not a guess
- premise: the old 0.85 compact-threshold was over-conservative — an enormous amount of good work happens between 85% and 95% in a FOCUSED session, and the handoff refresh alone measured at ~1% of context. A guessed headroom wastes the most productive stretch of a window.
- requirement: the ritual stamps `HANDOVER_START` and `HANDOVER_END` markers into the transcript; the retrospective dusk-parse ([SPEC:CXC-RETRO] §5a/§5b) correlates them with the context-% trajectory to compute `handover_cost_pct` into SQLite. Over sessions this MEASURES the headroom the threshold needs.
- threshold: `intelligence/meta/architect.meta.json` `lifecycle.compact_threshold` — the default hint for when to START the ritual (currently 0.93, data-collection). As `handover_cost_pct` accumulates, RAISE toward 0.95 if the cost stays ~1%. The Configuration-tab slider is the tuning surface; SQLite informs it. JUDGMENT ALWAYS OVERRIDES — wrap early when decohering.
- part-of: [SPEC:HANDOVER-PROCESS]

---

## 2. The process as a flow (for the human eye)

### [HANDOVER-PROCESS-FLOW] The crossing as an ordered, measured flow — mermaid-renderable
- definition: a linear ritual bracketed by two measurement stamps, then a SEPARATE fire. The ordered process, as flow steps:
    1. `trigger` (BRANCH) — context reaches the threshold (~0.93) OR judgment says wrap early (a meandering/decohering session). Either path enters the ritual.
    2. `stamp-START` — `echo HANDOVER_START <iso8601>` — the measurement boundary opens.
    3. `step-1-refine-dusk-gifts` — only if this session earned a NEW angle (a falsified instinct, a lesson with registration-shape). Not every session. (`bootstrap/dusk-gifts/`)
    4. `step-2-refresh-handoff` — `docs/intelligence-console/DESIGN-HANDOFF.md`: what landed, the current OPEN/PENDING, and retire any stale "do next" that actually shipped (or me.next re-builds done work).
    5. `step-3-reconcile-decision-graph` — advance each raised/open node to its CORRECT lifecycle-position, VERIFY-THEN-ADVANCE (check git/code/tests that it shipped BEFORE advancing; never on assumption). This is why the boot read's derived open-list can be trusted — the graph stops lying about what is done.
    6. `step-4-enrich-artifact-backlog` — fill the semantic fields of EVERY `NEEDS-ENRICHMENT` deliverable (not just this session's), grounded in what the artifact ACTUALLY is; never invent. The crossing is where the enrichment debt is paid down.
    7. `step-5-run-archivist` — the decision-archivist (dusk-aide mode) as the completeness backstop if decisions were made but not captured inline; ratify its dangles, do not re-author.
    8. `step-6-author-direction` — the custom /compact direction for THIS crossing: POINTER style (name the load-bearing artifacts to read + re-register), never an inline summary the summarizer would distort, never a stored template.
    9. `step-7-pre-persist-direction` — write the direction to `docs/compact-summaries/<crossing>/direction.md` (the summarizer never reads disk; the pointer + the successor's cold read carries the depth).
    10. `stamp-END` — `echo HANDOVER_END <iso8601>` — the measurement boundary closes.
    11. `fire` (SEPARATE) — fire the self-directed /compact (`{cmd:compact,direction:...}` on the out channel) as its own deliberate act, once prep is done and confirmed. NOT part of the ritual — the ritual preps + measures.
- measurement-edge: `stamp-START` and `stamp-END` both feed the SQLite `handover_cost_pct` metric that tunes [HANDOVER-IS-MEASURED]'s threshold — the flow's two brackets are also its instrumentation.
- mermaid-view: rendered for the human in the artifact `docs/factlattice/bootstrap-and-handover-flows.md` (Artifacts surface). lts_flow ([LEC-RENDER]) can regenerate the diagram from this node's step structure — the steps are authoritative; the mermaid is a projection.
- relates-to: [HANDOVER-IS-MEASURED], [SBR-PROCESS-FLOW], [SBR-ZEALOUS-CONTRIBUTION]
- part-of: [SPEC:HANDOVER-PROCESS]

---

## 3. The reciprocal

### [HANDOVER-IS-THE-DUSK-OF-THE-BOOT-READ] Every step here feeds a slice there
- definition: the handover is not bookkeeping — it is the deliberate authoring of what the next boot read will consume. Step 3 (reconcile the graph) makes slice 2 (OPEN/awaiting-me) TRUE. Step 4 (enrich artifacts) makes the Artifacts surface honest. Steps 1/6/7 (dusk gifts + direction) are what slice 5 (DUSK-GIFT ENGAGEMENT) reasons over. A crossing done well is a boot read that lands; a crossing skipped is the discover-as-you-go the boot read exists to end. Boot READS the corpus; dusk WRITES it — and the writing is this ritual.
- relates-to: [SPEC:SESSION-BOOTSTRAP-READ], [SBR-ZEALOUS-CONTRIBUTION], [SBR-STRUCTURE]
- part-of: [SPEC:HANDOVER-PROCESS]
